WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:08.426
An Istanbul business needs connectivity. Follow one order, with clear owners, explicit exceptions, and human decisions.

00:00:08.576 --> 00:00:15.477
This is a simulator. Amber production paths are proposals, not implemented features.

00:00:16.227 --> 00:00:22.164
Intake persists the order and event together. A stable key prevents duplicate work.

00:00:22.314 --> 00:00:26.668
Invalid requests return to the submitter, not downstream agents.

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:34.509
Validation checks the site and capacity before planning. Bad references stop for customer confirmation.

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:40.188
No capacity means manager review or rejection. Approval cannot invent inventory.

00:00:45.227 --> 00:00:51.796
Decomposition converts approved products into linked service and resource orders, reducing rekeying errors.

00:00:51.946 --> 00:00:57.869
Unsupported products are rejected at intake. Production planners must approve new catalogue mappings.

00:01:02.227 --> 00:01:08.275
Provisioning rechecks capacity and policy, then allocates once. A timeout activates recovery.

00:01:08.425 --> 00:01:14.317
Route risk or a closed change window stops before allocation, for a manager decision.

00:01:19.227 --> 00:01:25.767
Recovery handles one allowlisted partner timeout, retries once, and returns to provisioning.

00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:33.012
Unknown faults or exhausted retries need a proposed human triage path, not broader autonomous authority.

00:01:36.227 --> 00:01:43.637
The service manager owns high-risk decisions. Approval is audited, bounded, and cannot fabricate capacity.

00:01:43.787 --> 00:01:48.660
Approved work resumes its saved stage. Partners cannot approve.

00:01:52.227 --> 00:01:58.071
Customer updates persist bilingual portal status after activation, reducing avoidable chasing.

00:01:58.221 --> 00:02:05.949
External delivery failure needs a proposed service-desk path. This demo sends no SMS or email.

00:02:09.227 --> 00:02:19.184
Early checks prevent downstream errors. Linked identifiers remove rekeying. Persisted handoffs and bounded recovery reduce waiting.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:27.486
Under seven days and eight percent fallout are targets, not results. Measure lead time, first-time-right completion, and human-review waiting.

00:02:29.227 --> 00:02:38.422
TMF-inspired interfaces and MCP preserve interoperability. The proposed Azure Local workload keeps customer data in Turkiye.

00:02:38.572 --> 00:02:46.613
External metadata and services need approval. Stricter rules require eligible disconnected operation, not a live cloud link.
